Do not call libcaca's internal _caca_alloc2d() from img2txt/cacaview

img2txt and cacaview (src/common-image.c) call _caca_alloc2d(), a function
internal to libcaca that is not part of its API. libcaca is built with
-fvisibility=hidden wherever the compiler supports it (QNX's GCC does), so the
symbol is not exported from libcaca.so and the programs fail to link with
"undefined reference to `_caca_alloc2d'". Allocate the pixel buffer in the
program itself, with the same multiplication-overflow check.

Upstream-Status: Pending (not QNX-specific: any build with -fvisibility=hidden)

--- a/src/common-image.c
+++ b/src/common-image.c
@@ -161,7 +161,11 @@
     uint32_t depth = (bpp + 7) / 8;
 
     /* Allocate the pixel buffer */
-    im->pixels = _caca_alloc2d(im->w, im->h, depth);
+    /* _caca_alloc2d() is internal to libcaca (hidden by -fvisibility):
+     * allocate here, with the same overflow check. */
+    im->pixels = (im->w && im->h && (size_t)im->w * im->h / im->h == (size_t)im->w
+                  && (size_t)im->w * im->h * depth / depth == (size_t)im->w * im->h)
+                 ? malloc((size_t)im->w * im->h * depth) : NULL;
     if (!im->pixels)
     {
         caca_file_close(f);
